cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
title: "shMARL: multi-agent reinforcement learning for iterated games on graphs"
abstract: >-
  Simulation code for studying the emergence of cooperation among deep
  reinforcement learning agents playing the two-player Iterated Prisoner's
  Dilemma over synthetic graph topologies, with and without partner selection
  and opponent identity information.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/geronest/shMARL"
